    "narrative": "The strongest play in the LawDog lineup today is **Daulton Varsho**, who clears our board with a 65.17 efficiency score. His matchup against Lugo is the primary driver, as the dynamic platoon advantage against a right-handed starter boosts his ceiling, and his ability to exploit the high stolen base allowance against this specific opposing battery keeps him as a core anchor for our 5x5 objectives. While **Yainer Diaz** and **Kyle Karros** both hover near the 58-point mark, they lack the multi-category upside that **Daulton Varsho** brings to the table, particularly given that **Kyle Karros** faces the difficult King, M, whose pitch mix slightly stifles his aggressive base-running upside.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Zack Gelof**, who ultimately missed the cut with a 38.33 score, failing to breach our 40.0 baseline floor. Despite a favorable opponent in Rasmussen, the deep degradation of the SP skill metric combined with a detrimental park factor pushed **Zack Gelof** into the \u201cbelow floor\u201d category, signaling that a benching is the correct move to preserve our game caps. Meanwhile, we are monitoring the bottom of the order where **Braden Montgomery** enters with a marginal 44.45; while he is currently active, his position at the nine-hole combined with a tough left-handed opponent makes him a candidate for mid-game substitution if our bench assets like **Matt Chapman** or **Dylan Beavers** move into better situations.\n\nThe primary risk profile for LawDog today centers on our exposure to the McLean matchup. Both **Bryce Harper**, **Luis Arraez**, and **Justin Crawford** face this arm; while **Bryce Harper** maintains a solid 57.53 score due to his elite xwOBA, the combination of a pitcher with a 3.77 xERA and adverse park factors mandates that we monitor the game flow closely. We are currently sitting **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, and **Tyler Freeman** due to either schedule inactivity or minor league assignment, and we will continue to rely on the depth of **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Gavin Sheets** to supplement our output should **Gleyber Torres** or **Jonathan Aranda** fail to capitalize on their second-order lineup spots today.",
